</ul><h1>It's Time</h1><p><strong>How to use your Gianello Interchangeable 3-Strap Watch Set</strong></p>
<hr />
<ol>
<li>
<p>Choose which strap best matches your look for the day.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Attach it to the attractive watch face.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Look stylish and know what time it is.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Attend a long, boring work seminar.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>After being released, loiter in the halls with your coworkers, discussing what a drag it was.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>When someone says, “Gosh, that felt like forever! What time is it?” dramatically look at your watch and say, “Hey, it’s five o’clock somewhere! How about grabbing a happy hour drink?”</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Laugh softly to yourself.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Realize you are the only one laughing.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Realize no one is even <em>smiling</em>. Everyone else is looking at you, aghast.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Listen as your cubicle neighbor speaks up and says, “But it’s 4:43. There’s nowhere in the world that’s exactly 17 minutes ahead of us.”</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Watch as the circle of your coworkers, many of whom you would’ve considered friends, closes to exclude you.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Slip away.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Get in your car.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Drive.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>When you get to your exit, don’t turn off. Keep going.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>End up in a small idyllic town within the same time zone as your previous city.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Establish residence.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Pay a child to help you stage a series of do-gooder stunts: saving him from “almost drowning” in a river, retrieving a cat that “gets stuck” up a tree, rescuing a deaf dog who “just decided” to take a nap on the train tracks.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Parlay the goodwill into local celebrity status.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>With your newfound fame, launch a campaign for mayor, running on a platform of fixing potholes, strengthening schools, setting the time exactly 17 minutes ahead, and rejuvenating local parks.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Win in a landslide.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Serve as mayor.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>When the boy says he needs more money to keep quiet, skim a little bit off the budget for snow removal equipment.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>The next winter, after a blizzard ravages the area, feign ignorance as to why the roads remain clotted with snow for weeks.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>When an investigative journalist asks for your comment on budget inconsistencies, pay her off with money set aside for garbage truck repairs and maintenance.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Get impeached.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Try not to laugh when you realize the reason for your impeachment is not because the streets are impassable, blocked by either snow or piles of trash that the broken-down garbage trucks cannot pick up, but rather, the confusion around your mandated time change. Everyone’s tired of having to do the mental math whenever they leave town.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Flee.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Get your old job back.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Attend another long, boring seminar.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>This time, when someone asks what time it is as you leave, say, “It’s five o’clock somewhere,” but don’t laugh or smile.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Lock eyes with your former cubicle neighbor (you sit somewhere else now), daring them to defy you.</p>
</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<p>NOTE: Steps 4 through 32 are optional.</p>